# Generated files — leave them exactly as their generator writes them.
#
# `payload migrate:create` rewrites src/migrations/index.ts in its own style
# (semicolons). Reformatting it makes the file diverge from the generator, so
# the *next* migration re-emits all ~30 import lines and buries the one real
# change in a wall of noise.
#
# The others below are committed in their generator's format too (verified:
# `prettier --check` reports all of these as "would rewrite"), so formatting one
# would produce the same whole-file churn on its next regeneration. This list
# mirrors the generated files already ignored in eslint.config.mjs.
src/migrations/
src/payload-types.ts
src/app/(payload)/admin/importMap.js

# Protected paths. Claude Code never auto-approves a write under `.claude/` or
# to `.mcp.json`, so an unattended run cannot clear a formatting failure here:
# it waits on a prompt nobody answers (WeMeditateWeb#97). Gating them would
# make the gate unfixable by the loop, not merely inconvenient. `.claude/` is
# already ignored in eslint.config.mjs for its own reasons.
.claude/
.mcp.json

# pnpm writes this. Reformatting it makes the next `pnpm install` churn it back.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Seed data dumps, emitted as `JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)` by
# seeds/extract-to-json.ts and seeds/atlas/extract.ts.
seeds/atlas/data/
seeds/**/data*.json

# The canonical block here is compared against the copies in the other three
# product repos, modulo whitespace only
# (claude-workflow/workflow/lib/comment-rule-sync.mjs). Prettier rewrites
# `*why*` to `_why_`, which that check reads as drift — measured: it reported
# the other three repos DRIFTED. Formatting this file means formatting all four
# copies and the canonical source in one change.
docs/rules/code-comments.md
